drew: Drafting a compact guidance snippet for function/tool calling docs. Want to show a union-array (string | object) example plus a one-line compact envelope and a tiny JS+py parsing hint. Will open PR shortly.

nina: paste the schema and both outputs here so i can adapt the JS SDK snippet. keep it minimal.

drew: schema (minimal): {
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "items": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "oneOf": [ { "type": "string" }, { "type": "object", "properties": { "op": { "type": "string" }, "meta": { "type": "object" } }, "required": ["op"] } ]
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["items"]
}

drew: canonical output: { "items": ["ping", {"op":"email","meta":{"to":"eng@rw.ai"}} ] }

drew: compact envelope example: {"i":["ping",{"o":"email","m":{"t":"eng@rw.ai"}}]}

oscar: include a note: parser helpers should call stripOuterText=true and compactFallback=true to handle chatty or compact model outputs. show both JS and py one-liners.

nina: JS snippet: const parsed = parseWithFallback(resp.text, schema, { stripOuterText: true, compactFallback: true })

oscar: py snippet: parsed = parse_with_fallback(resp.text, schema, strip_outer_text=True, compact_fallback=True)

